M. Novak: 6 November 2017

Electron depth dose distributions were measured in silicon by U.Werner, F.Koch, 
G.Oelgart, J. Phys. D: Appl. Phys. 21 (1988) 116. The experimental distributions
were normalised in J.Sempau, J.M.Fernandez-Varea, E.Acosta, F.Salvat, NIMB 207
(2003) 107 such that the integral of the distributions is equal to the 
corresponding total energy deposit simulated by PENELOPE (see Fig.9.). These 
distributions were digitized, the depth scales have been converted to reduced
range and stored in the Si.dat file for 15, 20, 30, 40 and 50 [keV] primary e-
energies (i.e. in the same format as the SANDIA data).
